A||||12||GodSend||What to do before emissions test?||||1||
Z||000000||GodSend||11-15-2001||09:15 AM||||I have an e-test coming up soon, and would like to pass on the first shot.<P>My 87 GT runs nice , but has a slight idle hunting (900-1000 rpms).  I do get a check engine light every once and awhile at highway speeds.  Here is what I have replaced in the last little while.<P>Air Filter, Cap & Rot, O2 sensor, egr tube & gaskets (new from Dealer about 3 weeks ago, ugh!), 180 degree therm & rad cap.<P>I have my old 195 therm still laying around, will dropping that in allow the engine to run warmer and therefor less emissions?  I also plan on filling her up with premium.<P>Any other tips guys?  Thanks a bunch!||||reg||1
Z||000001||johnt671||11-15-2001||09:20 AM||||Yes, go with the 195 thermostat as the car will run leaner with it.<p>[This message has been edited by johnt671 (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||11-15-2001||09:23 AM||||Why the ENGINE light?  You never say, specifically.  Is it fixed after all the other changes?  If not, why not?<P>Be sure to change your oil and filter before such a test, also!||||reg||5
Z||000003||87GTZ34||11-15-2001||09:39 AM||||The check engine light at highway speeds is msot likely the EGR.  There is a feedback to the ECM (on the EGR switch) that tells it yes I opened, and if that switch is flakey you will get the light.  This feedback only detects if there is a vacuum leak in the line or EGR valve itself, it doesn't really know that the valve opened.  My EGR switch is flakey and I plugged the vacuum to it until I can get it replaced and its hit or miss as to the SES coming on.  If they need to run the car on the rollers, the a true EGR may cause you to fail but I would try it anyway.  The 195 therm will put less fuel in but not that much.  If your engine is not in that good of shape then do it.  The main thing is to take the car for a good long/somewhat spirited run right before you drive it to the testing center to make sure it is thoroughly warmed up.  Oh one more thing, 'pray'.||||reg||1
Z||000004||starfighter007@msn.com||11-15-2001||10:44 AM||||And as Johnf said change your oil and filter.this will keep your hydro carbon readings very low.And I think I would also checkto see what trouble codes might be stored in your computer .Goodluck||||reg||1
Z||000005||AkursedX||11-15-2001||10:49 AM||||Put in a tank of the highest octane unleaded you can find, or use some sort of octane booster fuel additive.  <P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||GodSend||11-15-2001||12:35 PM||||If my ECM stores those codes, would that cause it to run rich even if the light does not come on? ....<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnF||11-15-2001||01:04 PM||||Huh?  <P>An ECM storing (or not storing) a code will not cause your engine to run rich or lean.  A stored code might tell YOU if there is a CONDITION which might cause the engine to run rich or lean.||||reg||1
Z||000008||72vinman||11-15-2001||01:40 PM||||It looks as if you have already done some of the key things already. You might also want to take it out for a nice drive (at least 30 mins) just prior to the test. This will ensure that it is warmed up real good.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigvin2_1.gif"> ||||reg||7
Z||000009||FieroRacer||11-16-2001||11:37 PM||||I had my dodge daytona score gross polluter status twice.  Replaced the cat, did a pretest, it failed.  Drove at about 75mph in second gear on the freeway to the test only station.  Passed with a few zeros!!  When I got the Nova, I did a nice 60mph run down a 7 mile deserted street in first gear, then into the smog shop, passed with flying colors.  When I take the GT in after repairs, It's going to get to play on the freeway first.  Anyone know an 85 automatic's top speed?  85mph!!!  I need to upgrade that.||||reg||1
Z||000010||grinthock||11-17-2001||07:55 AM||||Change your license to a rural address for a month.  <P>Get your sticker.<P>Change it back.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||11-17-2001||02:44 PM||||Pray?||||reg||1
Z||000012||GodSend||11-18-2001||01:23 AM||||Good news, I passed!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">..  I took her in for an oil and filter about 10 minutes before the test.  Threw in some +92 gas, and threw in a new air filter.<P>I also swapped back in the old (and not working therm) - this ensured that the engine was nice and warm :P.  Other then that the only thing I did was clear the ecm by disconnecting the battery.  <P> ||||reg||1
